usso has:attachment."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"Checks exactly which messages a Russo Plumbing filter would catch, before anything moves."}]]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":3}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Create a filter: From tony@russoplumbing.example, Skip the Inbox, Apply the label Vendors, and apply it to matching conversations."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"Old and new invoices land under Vendors automatically, so the inbox stays a to-do list."}]]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary-600 text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold","children":4}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900","children":"Snooze Grace's roof estimate question until tomorrow."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1","children":"You can't answer until the estimate arrives. Snooze brings it back when you can."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-primary-200 text-gray-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Result: "}],"Vendor mail sorts itself, and the inbox shows only what needs you today."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-gray-900 font-medium","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","children":"🔑 "}],"Search first, then turn a good search into a filter."]}]]}]]}]]}]
24:["$","div","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Knowledge Check"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","$L2d","0",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"How is a Gmail label different from a folder?","options":["A message can have several labels, and it can stay in the inbox","Labels delete mail after 30 days","Other people can see your labels","Labels only work on sent mail"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Labels work like tags. A folder holds a message in one place; labels can overlap.","optionRationales":["Correct.","Labels never delete anything; Trash empties after 30 days.","Only you can see your labels.","Labels work on any conversation."]}}],["$","$L2d","1",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Which search finds messages from Russo Plumbing that have attachments?","options":["russo attachment","from:russo has:attachment","has:russo from:attachment","subject:russo"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"from: names the sender and has:attachment requires an attachment.","optionRationales":["Plain words also match messages that just mention Russo Plumbing or attachments.","Correct.","The operators are swapped.","That only checks the subject line."]}}],["$","$L2d","2",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"You created a filter that skips the inbox, but last month's matching messages are still in your inbox. Why?","options":["Filters only work on Mondays","You didn't check Also apply filter to matching conversations","Filters only work in Outlook","The messages are too large"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Filters run on new mail. To sort existing mail too, check Also apply filter to matching conversations when you create it.","optionRationales":["Filters run on every new message.","Correct.","Gmail filters work in Gmail.","Size doesn't matter unless your filter checks size."]}}]]}]]}]
